[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. The reports merged into it describe
three different problems. The queued parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not known. Two of its three problems have no fix queued and no ticket of their own until
now. Each one now has its own ticket, linked in the table.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} repo="carlosorch/mega-s01e03-support-kb" />

The export repeats some rows because its pages overlap. The table counts each report id once.

## What each problem is

**`parser`.** The shared parser reads every date month first. A tenant that writes the day first
books 4 March and gets 3 April. It hits every tenant on file, through the app, email and the
booking-v2 form. This is the bug the queued fix is for.

**`hint`.** Booking-v3's date field prints the hint `MM/DD/YYYY`, but the form reads the date the
tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint says and the date comes out flipped. It only
happens through the `form` channel of the three tenants on booking-v3: alder.physio, copper.studio
and pale.harbour. Fixing the parser does not touch it. The hint or the form's reading has to change.

**`one-day`.** These dates move by one day, not by a day/month swap: "Tuesday 6 October showed as
Monday", "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday", "every booking in June is
one day off". That pattern points at time zones or a day boundary, not at date order. The desk
already listed these reports in `desk-notes.json` as a one-day move, then filed them under
`parser` by tenant. The parser fix will not close them.

## How the reports were placed

- Tenant, locale and booking form decide `parser` vs `hint` (`causes.ts`). The intake tag does not,
  because intake guesses from the reporter's browser and gets it wrong often. The table shows the
  drift in the "tagged as" column.
- A report listed in `desk-notes.json` as a one-day move is `one-day`, whatever its tenant.
- Same subject line is not the same problem. Subjects like "Date is wrong" appear under all three.
  Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges by subject, and that is how three
  problems ended up in one ticket.

## What changes for the desk

- Reopen #4471 as the `parser` ticket only. Move the other two problems to their own tickets.
- When a report comes in about dates, check the tenant's form and the body before merging, not the
  subject.
- The counts above come from the data at render time. When the desk exports again, rebuild the page.

